Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Count the Apple A8 as supported

The A8's GPU (BVNC 3.10.4.5) runs Vulkan and, through Zink, the GLES
desktop on the iPod touch 6, and passes the probe, Vulkan and display
checks on the iPhone 6 and the iPad mini 4. Bind to it without
powervr.exp_hw_support, as to the A9's and the A10's, so an installed
system's desktop finds the GPU on every boot of a board that enables its
node; the login's GPU probe still falls back to the software desktop if
it does not draw.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
index 01f9f6041c..54e51102e1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -542,6 +542,7 @@ pvr_gpu_support_level(const struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(13, 10, 6, 2):	/* Apple A10 (T8010) */
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(9, 15, 6, 2):	/* Apple A9 (S8003) */
+	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(3, 10, 4, 5):	/* Apple A8 (T7000) */
 		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;

 	default:
